          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#general General
          %p
            An
            %strong affine scheme
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            that as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{op}
            of commutative
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            picture an affine scheme is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+space"} locally ringed space
            which is isomorphic to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+spectrum"} prime spectrum
            of a commutative ring. Affine schemes form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Scheme
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff\hookrightarrow Scheme
            of the category of schemes.
          %p
            The correspondence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\mapsto Spec(\Gamma_Y \mathcal{O}_Y)
            extends to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Scheme
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Scheme\to Aff
            %strong fundamental theorem on morphisms of schemes
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#IsbellDuality"} below
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Scheme
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CRing(R, \Gamma_Y\mathcal{O}_Y) \cong Scheme(Y, Spec R).
          %p
            In other words, for fixed
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            there is a restricted functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Scheme
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Aff
                        %mi op
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Aff
                        %mi op
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi CRing
                  %mo :
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Scheme(-,Y)|_{Aff^{op}} = h_Y|_{Aff^{op}} = h_Y|_{CRing} : CRing\to Set,
          %p
            and the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\mapsto h_Y|_{CRing}
            from schemes to presheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
          %p
            There is an analogue of this theorem for relative
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+scheme"} noncommutative scheme
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              There is no similar equation the other way round, that is “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi Scheme
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing(\Gamma_Y\mathcal{O}_Y, R) \cong Scheme(Spec R, Y)
              ” is not true in general. As a mnemonic, note that with ordinary
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection"} Galois connection
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection#properties"} homming into (not out of)
              the functorial construction. More geometrically, consider the example
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \mathbb{P}^n
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing(\Gamma_Y\mathcal{O}_Y, R)
              only contains the unique ring homomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℙ
                            %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℙ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^n}(\mathbb{P}^n) \cong \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Scheme
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Scheme(Spec R, Y)
              consists of all the
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^n
              (of which there are many).
          %h3#relative_affine_schemes Relative affine schemes
          %p
            A
            %strong relative affine scheme
            over a scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+scheme"} relative scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            isomorphic to the spectrum of a (commutative unital) algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in the category of quasicoherent
            = succeed "-modules;" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\subset Y
            the inverse image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}V\subset X
            is an open affine subscheme of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            isomorphic to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A(V))
            and such open affines glue in such a way that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi V
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}V\hookrightarrow f^{-1}W
            corresponds to the restriction morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(W)\to A(V)
            of algebras.
          %p
            Relative affine scheme is a concrete way to represent an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+morphism"} affine morphism
            of schemes.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#IsbellDuality Isbell duality
          #AffineSchemesFullSubcategoryOfOppositeOfRings.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
                form
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Schemes
                      %mi Aff
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Schemes_{Aff}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Ring^{op}
            %p
              from affine schemes to their global
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings+of+functions"} rings of functions
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hartschorne77"} Hartschorne 77, chapter II, prop. 2.3
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
                between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AffineSchemesFullSubcategoryOfOppositeOfRings"}
              is the analog in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              of similar statements of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Milnor%27s+exercise"} Milnor's exercise
          %div
